<!--
  An invented month, built for the two things build 006 fixes.

  ## One counterparty printed two ways (03 §3.9, §3.13)

  Two payments to a shop the terminal names "TESTHOEK 13" on one line and
  "TESTHOEK - 990311 Testref" on the next, because it appended a reference to
  the second. Build 005 read those as two counterparties and drew two names. They
  are one, the reference is per-transaction material, and §3.9 is explicit that
  a resolver may ignore it when deciding whether two records are the same
  counterparty.

  ## Filing without being told (03 §11.10-§11.14)

  Six more entries, chosen so that every branch of the classification is
  exercised on a real budget rather than only in a unit test:

    two card payments to a supermarket   -> Groceries
    a direct debit to a network operator -> Phone & Internet
    the bank's own charge                -> Bank fees, from the payment class
    a shop nothing knows about           -> stays Uncategorised
    money coming in                      -> stays Uncategorised

  The last two are the point of the file as much as the first three: §11.13
  would rather leave a transaction unfiled than have AYQ claim to know where it
  belongs, and a credit could be salary, a refund nobody flagged, or a friend
  paying back dinner.

  Every account, name, IBAN, terminal, amount and date here belongs to nobody.
  The two merchant names that are real companies are here because the
  classification is built on names of that kind and a test of it needs one; no
  transaction below ever happened.
-->
